## Gotchas learned today
- npm start and the installed app serve the LAST SUCCESSFUL build. A
  failed build means old code. Test fixes in npm run dev.
- vitest does not type-check. Run tsc; the build fails on type errors.
- console.debug lines need "Verbose" ticked in the console levels.
- A hook after an early return crashes the page. Happened 3 times.
- Spotify track objects carry `track: true`; never test for a `track`
  key to detect a wrapper.
- With Spotify shuffle on, a uris list starts at random unless the
  request gives an offset.
- Images inside a zero-width box need max-w-none.
- Installed app: a new start page or id needs uninstall + reinstall.
  Never change the manifest id after she installs.
- Git Bash and PowerShell need different commands.
- AGENTS.md: nothing new in SpotifyPlayerUI.tsx; no component over 400
  lines; playback position never in React state; no effect depending
  on what it updates; animate transform and opacity only; no unmeasured
  performance claims; type tokens only.

